\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture of the MMSAR evaluation framework. Visible RGB video streams are synthesized from scenario text prompts using multimodal large language models (Google Gemini 3.8 Flash and xAI Grok with spatial upscaling to $1280 \times 720$). A 256-level lookup table (\texttt  {melo\_lut}) transfers pseudo-thermal styling to emulate synchronized thermal infrared streams. Dual streams undergo $2\times $ square tiling ($640 \times 640$), video-level bounding box annotation in Label Studio, and 24~Hz frame extraction. Curated sequences are partitioned into 240-frame episodes under Option B (parent-video grouped split) with non-adjacent shuffling to prevent spatial data leakage. At edge inference, parallel lightweight YOLO11n detectors process incoming RGB and thermal frames at 24~Hz ($T_s \approx 41.7$~ms), combined with a late fusion max gate ($s[n] = \max (c_{\text  {RGB}}[n], c_{\text  {Thermal}}[n])$) and evaluated across six lightweight temporal decision methods ($W = 5$ frames, 208~ms latency bound).}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_architecture}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
